{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>They journeyed.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] says that the reason for mentioning 'on the fifteenth day of the second month' is to make known that Israel left Egypt on a Thursday. Now, the first day of the month of Nisan was a Thursday, and Iyar [began on] Friday and Sabbath, and behold, on the Sabbath day they came to the wilderness of Sin and complained when they encamped, and Moses told them that 'you shall eat meat in the evening,' and in the morning the manna descended. Now it is fitting that it be a Sunday, because he said 'and it shall be on the sixth day' (verse 5)—for it was the sixth day and the sixth of the manna's descent. What the Gaon said, we accept for the tradition's sake, not for his explanation—for who told him that the manna descended on the day after they came to the wilderness of Sin? Perhaps they stayed there four days or more, and the manna began to fall on a Sunday, for from the day of its descent it began to be counted. For all the nations rely on Israel in this count. Now, the uncircumcised called the names of the days of the week after the names of the planets, but the day of Sabbath—not so. And in the Arabic tongue they called five days by way of number, and the sixth day al-jumʿa, after their gathering, for it is for them the honored day of the week, and the day of Sabbath they called Sabt, for the shin and samekh interchange in their writing—and these they learned from Israel. Now, the people of India, who do not acknowledge the work of Creation, the beginning of the days of the week for them is Wednesday, because the star of that day is the star of the sun, and it has dominion over them according to their words."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Reading אלגומ\"ע as al-jumʿa (Arabic الجمعة, 'the gathering/Friday'), and סב\"ת as Sabt (Arabic السبت, 'Sabbath/Saturday'); the shin/samekh interchange refers to the Arabic transliteration conventions."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:03.054399460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}